From 6191978993a7bd29b80fc23e0d2e6058fe7f4252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/33] perf(chonk): parse step bytecode on a background thread
 during CLI proving

ChonkAPI::prove parsed each step's ACIR bytecode serially (ChonkLoad) between
accumulations. A background thread now parses the bytecode of every step in
step order while earlier steps are being accumulated; the main thread only
waits for a step's parse if it is not ready yet (in practice only step 0).

ChonkLoad and the CLI share chonk_load_constraints for installing a parsed
circuit into the request. Bytecode parsing draws no randomness, and the witness
(whose gap filling does) is still parsed in order by ChonkAccumulate, so the
order of RNG draws and the transcript are unchanged. NO_MULTITHREADING builds
parse inline.
---
 .../cpp/src/barretenberg/api/api_chonk.cpp    | 90 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../src/barretenberg/bbapi/bbapi_chonk.cpp    | 27 ++++--
 .../src/barretenberg/bbapi/bbapi_chonk.hpp    | 10 +++
 3 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

